WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.420
A published study compared
twenty-three countries.

2
00:00:03.470 --> 00:00:06.530
Across: chocolate eaten per person.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:10.310
Up: Nobel prize winners
per ten million people.

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.410
The dots climb from
bottom left to top right.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.320
The correlation coefficient is
nought point seven nine one.

6
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.590
So should you eat more chocolate?

7
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.620
Or is the link just a fluke?

8
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.350
In this mission, you'll describe a
correlation by its direction and its strength.

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.200
You'll use a regression line to predict,
and see why extrapolation is risky.

10
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:35.530
And you'll ask what a scatter diagram
alone can tell you about cause.

11
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.770
Your mission: decide whether
you should eat more chocolate.
